            class Xform "ScrubBirch_F" (
                doc = "Birch sapling. Self-seeds into ballast, gravel and cracked slab faster than anything else in this climate, and its open airy crown silhouettes completely differently from the dense mounds around it. The white bark is graded to 0.036 - it is a pale trunk, not a light source. Aerial-perspective variant: beyond 100 m - more saturation removed, value dropped and the residue pushed cool, so the band reads as a silhouette layer behind the haze rather than a pale smear glowing through it. Asset Gray_Birch (3.332 m native), height band 1.80-3.30 m."
