        def Scope "GroundGrit" (
            doc = "Half-buried grit and stone, 80-190 mm, on the lee (ENE) side of every windward face, in the trench drain and at the weed lines. Round 6 replaced 1440 autumn leaf drifts with this: the drift POSITIONS were right - they came from a wind-lee model - but crisp orange oak and maple leaves put the level in October while the sky, the grass and the trees put it in August."
        )
